/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2018-11-07T21:11:28Z","updated_at":"2019-01-16T17:08:19Z","closed_at":"2019-01-16T17:08:19Z","author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> ATTENTION! Please read and follow:\r\n> - if this is a _question_ about how to build / test / query / deploy using Bazel, ask it on StackOverflow instead: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/bazel\r\n> - if this is a _discussion starter_, send it to bazel-discuss@googlegroups.com\r\n> - if this is a _bug_ or _feature request_, fill the form below as best as you can.\r\n\r\n### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\nWhen a sandboxed action fails and the user specified --verbose_failures, Bazel \"helpfully\" prints the full command that actually failed, e.g.:\r\n\r\n`(cd /home/user/.cache/bazel/_bazel_user/abcdef/execroot/name &&   exec env -     LD_LIBRARY_PATH=''     PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/opt/bin     PWD=/proc/self/cwd     TMPDIR=/tmp   /home/user/.cache/bazel/_bazel_user/abcdef/execroot/name/_bin/linux-sandbox -t 15 -w /home/user/.cache/bazel/_bazel_user/abcdef/sandbox/linux-sandbox/11/execroot/name -w /tmp -w /dev/shm -D -- /bin/bash)`\r\n\r\nThe path in the \"cd /home/user/...\" part is wrong - this should actually be the path of the sandbox where the action runs.\r\n\r\nTo fix this, we probably just have to print the `sandbox.getSandboxExecroot().getPathFile()` path instead of `execRoot.getPathFile()` here: https://source.bazel.build/bazel/+/ea4840042b0c087685ab4faffab58ba6906b06f5:src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/sandbox/AbstractSandboxSpawnRunner.java;l=136\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://a